# Father Donavich (docs/voice/donavich.md)

~ start
if flag.doru_destroyed and not flag.donavich_knows_fate
-> doru_dead_news
endif
if flag.doru_freed and not flag.donavich_knows_fate
-> doru_freed_news
endif
if attitude.donavich == hostile
-> hostile_again
endif
if flag.donavich_met
-> again
endif
set donavich_met
Narrator: A thin man in a threadbare vestment kneels at the altar, praying in a voice worn down to gravel. Beneath the floor, something answers him: a long, hungry cry.
Donavich [afraid]: Who... forgive me. Visitors. We have so few. The doors are open; I can't remember why I stopped barring them. Perhaps I hoped someone would come.
if flag.death_house_sacrificed
Donavich [afraid]: Forgive me, children. You've been in the house at the end of the lane; there's a smell on you I know from funerals that went wrong. That house wanted an offering. I won't ask what you gave it. The Morninglord already knows.
interject class:cleric: We'll answer for it. Not to you, Father. But we'll answer.
elif flag.death_house_refused
Donavich: The bell rang by itself when that house at the end of the lane began to groan. You were inside it, weren't you, children? And you came out. The Morninglord keeps odd company these days.
endif
if flag.death_house_children_riding
Narrator: He looks at you, then past you, at something just over your shoulder. His lips move: two small names, said like a blessing.
elif flag.death_house_children_at_rest
Donavich [sad]: The Durst children. Rose and Thorn. Folk saw them in the road for years. If they are at rest now, then you've done more for this village in a night than I have in a year.
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: A sunburst, this far into the dark. Someone kept faith here. Morning's grace on you for it, Father.
Narrator: From under the floor a young man's voice cries out, hoarse and eager: Father, who's there? I can smell them!
Donavich [afraid]: Forgive me. Pay it no mind, children, please. It's nothing that concerns you.
-> menu

~ again
if flag.doru_destroyed and flag.donavich_mercy_blessing
Donavich [sad]: It's still quiet below. I keep waking to listen for him. Habit, I suppose. Grief is mostly habit.
elif flag.doru_freed
Donavich [weary]: You've come back. He hasn't. I leave the side door unbarred at night now. I don't know if that's faith or foolishness.
elif flag.doru_left_locked
Donavich [weary]: You've come back. He's still below. You left him to me, and I'm grateful, and some nights I wish you hadn't. Both of those are prayers, I think.
else
Donavich: You've come back, children. Forgive me if I don't rise; my knees have taken the shape of the floor.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* [if not flag.doru_revealed] Who's screaming under the floor? -> screaming
* [if flag.doru_revealed and not flag.doru_destroyed and not flag.doru_freed] About your son. -> son_menu
* [if flag.burial_agreed and not flag.donavich_will_officiate and not flag.donavich_refused_rites and not flag.burgomaster_buried] Will you bury the burgomaster? -> burial
* [if not flag.holy_symbol_rumor] Is any relic of the Morninglord left in this valley? -> raven
* [Cleric] Kneel and pray with him. -> pray
* Is there anything you need? Anything you can spare? -> needs
* Goodbye. -> END

~ screaming
if flag.doru_spoken_to
Donavich [sad]: You've been below. You've seen him. Then there's no use lying, is there.
-> truth
endif
Donavich [afraid]: A madman. A poor soul I shelter, out of charity. He's loud. Please, don't go near the undercroft door.
* [Insight DC 10] That's no madman, Father, and you know it. -> truth | insight_fail
* [Persuasion DC 12] We can help. But you have to tell us the truth. -> truth | persuade_fail
* Then we'll sit with you, Father, until he goes quiet. -> screaming_vigil
* As you say. -> menu

~ screaming_vigil
time +120
Narrator: You sit in the back pews while he prays. The voice below begs, then bargains, then sings a hymn with the words wrong. Near the second hour it stops calling him Father and starts calling him Papa.
Donavich [sad]: Forgive me. You've sat through it now. There's no use lying to people who've sat through it.
-> truth

~ insight_fail
Narrator: He holds your gaze with the steadiness of a man who has rehearsed this every night. It may even be true; you can't tell.
-> menu

~ persuade_fail
Donavich [afraid]: There's nothing to tell. Nothing. Please.
-> menu

~ truth
set doru_revealed
quest the_priests_son heard
Donavich [sad]: My son. Doru. He went with the other young men to storm the castle and kill the devil in his bed. They had torches and a song. The devil gave them dinner.
Donavich: Months later Doru came home, at night, wearing his own face. I lured him below and barred the door. I pray. He screams. Neither of us has stopped since.
interject tag:pious: You've kept him from the village all this time. That took more strength than you know.
Donavich: Please. Whatever you are, don't hurt him. There may be a way back. There must be.
-> son_menu

~ son_menu
* [if not flag.doru_cure_promised] We'll look for a way to save him. -> promise_cure
* [if not flag.donavich_mercy_blessing and not flag.donavich_mercy_refused] Father, let us end his suffering. -> mercy
* [if not flag.undercroft_unbarred] We'd like to speak with him. Lift the bar. -> unbar
* Back to other matters. -> menu

~ promise_cure
set doru_cure_promised
set doru_left_locked
quest the_priests_son cure_promised
attitude donavich friendly
Donavich: You would? There are old stories. Saints' bones that turn the dead. Relics of the Morninglord. The sun itself, once. If anything in this valley could bring him back, it's one of those.
Donavich [sad]: I'll keep him fed on prayer until you come back. It's all I have to feed him on.
-> menu

~ mercy
Donavich [afraid]: End it. You mean kill him. Kill my boy.
* [Religion DC 13] What screams down there isn't Doru. His soul is caged. Let us free it. (one try) -> mercy_ok | mercy_fail
* [Persuasion DC 15] One night that bar will break. Let it end gently, before it does. (one try) -> mercy_ok | mercy_fail
* [Cleric] Speak to him as one priest to another. -> mercy_cleric
* Forget I asked. -> son_menu

~ mercy_cleric
Narrator: You don't argue. You tell him what you would want if it were your child, and what you would want if it were you down there, and he listens with his eyes closed.
-> mercy_ok

~ mercy_ok
set donavich_mercy_blessing
set undercroft_unbarred
attitude donavich friendly
Narrator: He's silent so long the candles gutter. When he speaks, his voice is very small.
Donavich [sad]: Do it, then. Gently, if there's any gentle way. I've lifted the bar. I can't watch. I'm sorry, my boy. I'm so sorry.
if not flag.donavich_gave_holy_water
set donavich_gave_holy_water
give holy_water 2
Donavich: Take these. Holy water. It will burn him. I blessed it for him weeks ago, and could never throw it.
endif
-> END

~ mercy_fail
set donavich_mercy_refused
Donavich [angry]: No. No! He's my son. You'll not touch him. The bar stays where it is, and you'll stay away from it.
-> menu

~ unbar
Donavich [afraid]: Talk? Oh, he'll talk. He'll talk you all the way to the door and through it. He was always good at talking.
* [Persuasion DC 12] Only talk. You have our word. -> unbar_ok | unbar_fail
* Then come down with us, Father, and keep your own hand on the bar. -> unbar_watched
* Never mind. -> son_menu

~ unbar_watched
time +60
Donavich [afraid]: My own hand. Yes. I've held it every night for months, from this side. First let me pray. An hour. Forgive me; I need the hour more than he does.
Narrator: When the hour is up he lifts the bar, and sits at the head of the stair with it across his knees, lips moving, ready to drop it back.
set undercroft_unbarred
-> menu

~ unbar_ok
set undercroft_unbarred
Donavich: Your word. In Barovia that's a strange coin. Very well; the bar is up. Don't open your hand to him. Don't let him see your throat.
-> menu

~ unbar_fail
Donavich [afraid]: No. I'm sorry. I can't. If he gets past you, he gets past me, and then the village. The bar stays.
-> menu

~ burial
if flag.doru_destroyed and not flag.donavich_mercy_blessing
Donavich [angry]: You ask me that? After what you did below? No.
set donavich_refused_rites
quest bury_the_burgomaster no_priest
-> END
endif
Donavich: Kolyan. He came every holy day until there were no holy days left. Yes. Yes, I'll say the words over him. It's the one thing I still know how to do.
Donavich [afraid]: Bring him to the grave behind the church; I'll meet you there. And if my boy cries out during the rites, keep singing. Please. Keep singing.
set donavich_will_officiate
quest bury_the_burgomaster priest_agreed
-> menu

~ raven
set holy_symbol_rumor
if name:hedda_ironvow and not (quest.cold_prayers >= the_symbol)
quest cold_prayers the_symbol
endif
Narrator: At the word relic, Donavich's hands stop shaking.
Donavich: The Holy Symbol of Ravenkind. Older than this church. A giant raven brought it to a paladin of the dawn, the stories say, and it was turned against the devil once, and lost after. Lost, mind. Not destroyed.
Donavich: If anyone alive knows where it lies, it's the old Vistani seer at Tser Pool. Or him. He keeps what frightens him.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Lost, not destroyed. Master Sorrel says nothing's ever lost. It's just being difficult.
-> menu

~ pray
attitude donavich friendly
Narrator: You kneel beside him and pray aloud. For a few breaths the voice under the floor stops, as if it's listening too.
Donavich [sad]: You still feel Him? Here? I haven't, not for a year. I say "Dawn will come" every night, to keep my mouth from saying other things.
-> menu

~ needs
Donavich: Need? Food. Sleep. My son back. You can't give me those, children. Holy water is all I have left to give, and precious little of that.
if flag.vestry_chest_opened
Donavich [weary]: Ah, but you've found the vestry chest already. Keep what you took. It does no good in a box.
elif not flag.donavich_gave_holy_water and attitude.donavich == friendly
set donavich_gave_holy_water
give holy_water 2
Donavich: Here. Two flasks. Throw them hard; the dead don't flinch the way the living do.
elif flag.donavich_gave_holy_water
Donavich: I've given you all I had. The well's dry, and so am I.
else
Donavich: The rest is in the vestry, for the burial of the dead. Ask me again when I know you better.
endif
-> menu

~ doru_dead_news
set donavich_knows_fate
quest the_priests_son doru_destroyed
if flag.donavich_mercy_blessing
Donavich [sad]: It's quiet. For the first time in weeks, it's quiet below. Thank you. I think. Ask me again in a year.
interject class:cleric: He's at rest, Father. Truly at rest. I'd stake my faith on it.
Donavich: Then he's farther from the castle than any of us. Go. Bury your dead. I'll bury mine.
-> END
endif
attitude donavich hostile
Donavich [angry]: You went down there. You killed my boy. I begged you. I begged you.
if not flag.burgomaster_buried
set donavich_refused_rites
quest bury_the_burgomaster no_priest
Donavich [angry]: Get out of my church. Bury your burgomaster yourselves. I have a son to bury, and no one to say the words over him either.
else
Donavich [angry]: Get out of my church.
endif
-> END

~ doru_freed_news
set donavich_knows_fate
attitude donavich indifferent
Donavich [afraid]: The bar is up. The undercroft is empty. You let him out. He'll go to the castle. He'll go to him.
Donavich [sad]: And Morninglord forgive me, the moment he was gone I slept, the first time in weeks. What kind of father sleeps?
-> menu

~ hostile_again
Donavich [angry]: There's nothing for you here. Not anymore. Go.
-> END
